  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Manufacturing Africa - Tanzania (ICF)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Manufacturing Africa (MA) is one of the UK&#x2019;s Centres of Expertise and works with African governments and international companies to attract large-scale Foreign Direct Investment (FDI) in the manufacturing sector. MA targets investment sizes from c. $2m-$20m. To date, regionally, MA has raised &#xa3;22 for every &#xa3;1 spent and aims to raise &#xa3;1.2bn by 2027. There have been 35 deals closed so far, generating of &#xa3;989mn of investment and 28,699 direct jobs. P4P has jointly-funded the expansion of MA into Tanzania with the MA central team since August 2023, with a specific focus on supporting investments that facilitate climate change mitigation and adaptation, and investments in agribusiness to increase food security. The programme aligns with P4P objectives to support improved productivity and structural transformation of the economy.</narrative>
  </description>
